1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=1707 '''Zeng Bu''' 曾布] [1707] Yuanyou coalition. Yizhan's [7363] son, Zhao's [7072] and Gong's [7364] brother, Yu(1)'s [1712] father, Chun's [1691] grandfather, Y
2 CONC i(2)'s [1704], Xun's [7362], Yu(2)'s [1713] and Xu's [7073] uncle, Jiang(1) Bao's [7193] father-in-law. He once recommended Peng(1) Ruli's [1400] younger brother, Rulin [3708]. According to Jingkou qijiu zhuan, 2.3a, after his dis
2 CONC grace, he and his younger brother Zhao moved to Zhenjiang, Dantu count (Zhenjiang). Zhao was buried in Nanfeng-s, but his sons and grandsons, including Tang [15462] (who was a Zhenjiang resident) and Tang's son, Wan [15461], who w
2 CONC as buried in Jintan, were Zhenjiang residents. Some of these descendants of Bu and Zao subsequently moved to Changzhou, which will only be indicated if documentary sources are found. Therefore, I am keeping Zhao and Gong as Nanfen
2 CONC g residents, Bu moves to Zhenjiang (where he purchased a residence when he was prefect) with his sons and nephews and other moves and residences follow the documented sources. XCB, 215.7b, 14a, 220.11a-11b, 225.2a, 246.13b, 247.1a
