1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=8136 '''Zeng Gongliang''' 曾公亮] [8136] His family claimed to be descendants of Zengzi, author of the Xiaojing, but this branch was not prominent until Song. Gongli
2 CONC ang's ancestors moved to Quanzhou, Jinjiang xian from Guangzhou, Gushi xian at end of Tang. Xiaokuan's [1695], Xiaoguang's [1696], Xiaozong's [1698] and Xiaoyun's [1700] father; Wei's [1710] granduncle; Chen(1) Yaozi's [99] son-in
2 CONC -law. Affinal relation of Tang(2) Xun [1595]. Brother of Wang(2) Ping's [1856] wife and father of Ren(1) Zhuan's [874] son-in-law, Zeng(1) Xiaozhang [3905]. In Qiang Zhi's funerary inscription for Zhu(1) Sun's [521] daughter, whos
2 CONC e husband is named as Zeng Jun, his sons, Xiaozhuo [3904] and Xiaozong(2) [3906], used their lineage uncle (shifu) Gongliang's yin to enter the civil service. Their address was Quanzhou, Jinjiang xian and they had the same generat
2 CONC ional name as Gongliang's sons. In Qiang Zhi's funerary inscription for Zeng(1) Gongwang [3908], he provides exactly the same information about wife and sons and son-in-laws, with the exception that Zeng(1) Xiaoyun [1700] is added
2 CONC  as a son (probably born of a concubine). It would, therefore, seem that Gongwang and Jun are, in fact, the same person, who was Qiang(1) Zhi's [7138] father-in-law. Another son-in-law, Du(3) Yin 3925] has the same generational na
2 CONC mes as the sons of Du(3) Yan [1730]. Zeng(1) Dang [1708] has the same generational name as Gongliang's grandsons. Gongliang's great great grandson, Chong [3900], was the father-in-law of Wei(5) Liangchen's [8158] son, Shujie [4002
2 CONC ]. Chong was buried in Suzhou, Wuxian. Chong's son, Qinian [7361], was buried in Suzhou, Changshu xian. Xiaoji [1693], Xiaoxu [1694], Xiaolian [1697] and Xiaoyou [1699] all have the same generational name as his sons and nephews. 
2 CONC His great grandnephew, Conglong [3911], was jinshi # 1 in 1199. He served on State council in 1215-1219 and again in 1234-35. Fujian TZ, 147.10b; Qiang Zhi, WJ, 35.4a-4b, 9b; Ouyang Xiu, WJ, 31.3b; Shen Shi san, 40.82a; Du Dagui, 
2 CONC 'zhong,' 52.1a-5b. CBD, 4, 2819-2822. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
