1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=8031 '''Jia Changchao''' 賈昌朝] [8031] His ancestors were Hedong jun Jia(3) descended from Jia Yi [3220] of the Han dynasty. His immediate ancestors during the Tang
2 CONC  lived in Cangzhou, Nanpi xian and then moved to Zhending, Huolu xian. Beginning with his father, Zhu [3219], this lineage branch of the clan buried their dead in Kaifeng. Yan's [448] grandnephew, Changheng's [435] elder brother, 
2 CONC Qing's [436] father, Chen(1) Yaozi's [99] and Wang(2) Zhen's [1776] son-in-law, father-in-law of Pang(1) Yuanying [1393], Cheng(1) Lin's [118] son, Sibi [3107], and Song(2) Qi(2)'s [1558] son, Huiguo [3797]. He was the elder broth
2 CONC er of Jia(3) Changqi [3217], who was the father-in-law of Wang(2) Ping's [1856] son, Jiong [3940]. Affinal relation of Tang(2) Xun [1595]. Wang Anshi, WJ, 87.902, Wang Gui, WJ, 56.1a-13b, 13b-15b (wife, born Chen, who died in 1067
2 CONC  at age 63). CBD, 4, 3082-83. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
