1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=1514 '''Sun Changqing''' 孫長卿] [1514] He used the yin of his maternal grandfather, Zhu(1) Sun [521], to enter the civil service. He lacked literary ability, but wa
2 CONC s strong in administrative matters (zhengshi). The funerary inscription for his wife does not include the mingzi for her patrilineal ancestors, but includes their titles, which identified Wang(2) Li [21274] as her father, whose fu
2 CONC nerary inscription lists Sun(1) Changqing as a son-in-law. Zhang(1) Hui(4)'s [7157] father-in-law. XCB, 188.7a; Wang Anshi, WJ, 100.1028-29 (wife, born Wang, who died in 1059 at age 53); Lu Dian, WJ, 15.19b-20a (identical to inscr
2 CONC iption for wife drafted by Wang(2) Anshi [1762] and Lu(5) Dian [8098] received the jinshi 11 years after her death; i.e., in some way Wang Anshi's draft inscription found its way into Lu Dian's collected papers); Shen Gou, WJ, 2.1
2 CONC 2b; SS, 331.1a-2a. Weiyang Z (1542), 22.34a-35b. CBD, 3, 1922. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
