1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=578 '''Fan Bailu''' 范百祿] [578] Posthumously purged as Yuanyou coalition member. A seventh generation ancestor migrated from Changan and was the first to be buried
2 CONC  in Chengdu, Huayang xian. His uncle Zhen's [3279] son-in-law was Wu(3) Anshi [7094] and his cousin Bailu(2)'s [3284] [Zhen's son] father-in-law was Yang(2) Hui [2007]. Bailu [578] was Baizhi's [7217] brother, Zuyu's [7026] uncle,
2 CONC  Zhao(1) Conggu's [7180] and Song(2) Duanping's [7346] son-in-law, and Xianyu(1) Chun's [7242] father-in-law. His cousin Baijia's [3283] (Zhen's son) father-in-law was Zeng(1) Xiaokuan [1695]. Zichang [3288], the nephew of his gre
2 CONC at grandson, was Hubei yunpan in 1210. Shi(1) Ji's [7330] nephew, Minzhan [3720], was the father-in-law of Fan(2) Zhonggu [3277], who had the same generational name as Bailu's great grandsons and great grandnephews. Fan Zuyu, WJ, 
2 CONC 39.14a, 44.1a-18a; XCB, 266.4a, 370.9b; SHY:ZG, 74.35a; SS, 337.9a; Su Shi, WJ, 'qianji,' 39.447. CBD, 2, 1646-7. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
