1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=14 '''Chao Duanyan''' 晁端彥] [14] Zongque's [8001] grandson, Zhongyan's [7119] son, but listed as a Jizhou, Juye resident. There were two brothers, Jiong [3012] and
2 CONC  Gou [3015], whose father, Quan [3011], moved from Chanzhou, Qingfeng xian to Kaifeng, Xiangfu xian and a lineage cousin, Di [3018], who was a Jizhou, Juye resident, who were the Song patriarchs of the separate branches of this li
2 CONC neage. Wang Anshi, for example, in the funerary inscription for Duanyan's lineage uncle, Zhongcan [3013], a Jizhou, Juye resident, links him to both Jiong and Zongque [8001] even though he was son of Zongjian [3021] and grandson o
2 CONC f Di. Zhongcan's son-in-laws include Fan(2) Chuncui [561] and Du(3) Chun [1724]. Lineage cousin Duanli's son-in-law, Ma(2) Chengxiu [3664], has the same generational name as Ma(2) Yuanfang's [1355] great grandsons and great grandn
2 CONC ephews. For more lineage information and linkages, see son Yuezhi's [3029] funerary inscription in Chao Yuezhi, WJ, 20.3b and also Chao(2) Zongke's [7121] biographical data. He received his jinshi in the same exam as Zhang(2) Dun 
2 CONC [333] and they also held appointments together in the same institutes. When Dun became chief minister and Duanyan saw what he was doing, he strongly criticized Dun and as a result was given a minor provincial post. Chao Buzhi, WJ,
2 CONC  62.27b; Chao Yuezhi, WJ, 19.23b; XCB, 333.10a, 335.12b, 341.7b, 350.11b-12a, 442.2b, 456.11a; SHY:ZG, 66.23b, 27a; Wang Anshi, WJ, 96.994. CBD has him as Duanlin's younger rather than elder brother, which is true based on their f
2 CONC ather, Zhongyan's funerary inscription. See documentation for Sheng(1) Guanzhong [13532] for identification of grandfather-in-law. CBD, 3, 1956-7. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
