1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=8100 '''Lü Yijian''' 呂夷簡] [8100] When Emperor Renzong [9004] (q.v.) took personal control over the government, Yijian and Renzong planned to dismiss from position
2 CONC s of power partisans of Yang(2) Huangtaihou [4215], regent during the emperor's minority. He was allied with the adopted son of Yan(4) Chenghan [2067] (qv.), Yan(4) Wenying [4117] during this period. Yijian was Mengheng's [7054] s
2 CONC on, Mengzheng's [8101] nephew, Jujian's [1300] cousin, Gongzhuo's [7304], Gongru's [1315], Gongzhu's [1314] and Gongbi's [1316] father, Xichun's [1304], Xiji's [1305], Xijie's [7303] and Xidao's [1306] grandfather, and Jiawen's [1
2 CONC 294] and Haowen's [8099] great grandfather. Yijian was the son-in-law of Fufeng jun Ma(2) Liang [1349] and father-in-law of Wang(2) Yong [7091]. LU(9) Xichang [1303] and Xicui [1307] have the same generational name as his grandson
2 CONC s and grandnephews. Zhang Fangping, WJ, 36.1a-11b. CBD, 2, 1202-3. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
