1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=4147 '''Zhang Xun''' 張] [4147] Documentation for descendant, Huan(3) [13664], documentation has his great grandson Xianzhen [13662] moving to Changzhou for the fi
2 CONC rst time, whereas Yu's [325] funerary inscription has Xun holding office in Changzhou and moving here. Since Piling zhi, 7.18b has Xun as prefect of Changzhou during the short period of the kingdom of Wu, I am assuming that Yu's i
2 CONC nformation is correct. Xun is also listed as the great grandfather of Wenzhi [318] and Xun's grandfather, Sheng(2) [12244], as the lineal ancestor of both Wenzhi, Yu, Shou(3) [8017] and Huan. There are some inconsistencies between
2 CONC  the various funerary inscriptions of these two branches of the lineage--particularly on when and where they moved between residence in Yangzhou and move to Changzhou, but all agree on the move, and data on Xun and Sheng. — [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
