1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=7385 '''Wang Yuan''' 王元] [7385] He used his uncle Zhi's [7079] yin to enter the civil service. Dan's [8153] grandson, Lun(2)'s [8178] grandfather, Yi(5)'s [7377] 
2 CONC father, Chao(2) Zhongyan's [7119] son-in-law. Since his first wife, Zhao(1) Anren's [8176] granddaughter, died at the age of 30 in 1063, his second wife Chao(2) Shi was no less than 22 years old when they married. Zhao(1) Shi prod
2 CONC uced six sons, but apparently no daughters before she died. His son-in-law, Huangfu(1) Shen [3423], had the same generational name as the son of Huangfu(1) Bi [868]. His son-in-law, Li(2) Shimou [3527], had the same generational n
2 CONC ame as the grandsons of Li(2) Zhaoshu [987]. Chao Buzhi, WJ, 67.10a-13a, 13a-14a (wife #1, born Zhao, who married him at age 16 and died in 1063 at age 30), 14a-15a (wife #2, born Chao, who died in 1093 at age 53). CBD, 1, 104. —
2 CONC  [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
