1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=13 '''Chao Buzhi''' 晁補之] [13] Yuanyou coalition. According to Zhang Lei's funerary inscription, the family descended from Chao Cuo, but there was no genealogical 
2 CONC record tracing the lineage between Han and the beginning of Song. Lei traces the Song lineage to Qingfeng residents, which firmly links both branches of the Chao, as does his following linkage of the Jiong->Zongque and the Zongjia
2 CONC n->Zhongyan(2)->Buzhi. Duanyou's [3025] son. Buzhi's sons are Gongwei [3017] and Gongsi [3016]. Du(3) Chun's [1724] son-in-law, father-in-law of Li(2) Zhi(4) [999] . Another son-in-law, Li(2) Xiangru [3500], was also the grandson-
2 CONC in-law of Chao(2) Qianzhi's [10] father. Buzhi's third younger sister was the wife of Yan(4) Xun's [2068]'s grandson, Shimeng [4115]. Another sister's husband, a Suzhou 1076 jinshi Zhang(1) Yuanbi [3178], has the same address and 
2 CONC generational name as Zhang(1) Mian's [262] grandsons. Yan(4) Deji [4116], the father-in-law of Chao(2) Buzhi's uncle, Duanben [3024], was probably kin with Yan(4) Xun [2068]. Yan(4) Shi married Duanben at the age of 19. She gave b
2 CONC irth to seven sons, none of whom reached maturity, and she died at the age of 65. Her son-in-law was Du(3) Chun's [1724] son, Du(3) Kai [3918]. Chao Buzhi, WJ, 68.11a; Zhang Lei, WJ, 12.17a; XCB, 478.7a; Huang Tingjian, WJ, 23.4b;
2 CONC  YLDD, 2368.4b; Du Dagui, zhong, 34.4b-6b. CBD, 3, 1953-4. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
