1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=1490 '''Su Qi''' 蘇耆] [1490] His ancestors were Wugong jun Su(1). The ancestor who fled to Sichuan at the time of the Guangming (880) troubles had three sons. The 
2 CONC eldest returned and became a great minister (xiang) of Tang. The second served in the Tang government. The youngest, Zhen [3756], remained in Sichuan as Tongling xian magistrate. This was Qi's great great grandfather. His great gr
2 CONC andfather and grandfather served in the administration of the Meng(2) kings of Shu. When Shu was incorporated into the Song empire, his grandfather continued as a Song official. Qi was Yijian's [8115] son, Shunyuan's [1505], Shunq
2 CONC in's [7064], and Shunbin's [7065] father, and Xie's [1501], Yi's [1502], Bi's [7340] and Zhu's [3755] grandfather. He was the son-in-law of Wang(2) Dan [8153] and Han(1) Zong [657], father-in-law of Han(1) Wei [8051], and brother-
2 CONC in-law of Wang(2) Su [1881]. Han Wei, WJ, 30.1a-3a (wife, born Wang, who died in 1041 at age 55); XCB, 108.9a, 116.11a; LPJ, 6.6a; Su Shunqin, WJ, 14.202. CBD, 5, 4308. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46
2 CONC 406 RMH]
