1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=17946 '''Qian Shouzhi''' 錢受之] [17946] Wang Yingchen, WJ, 23.285-6 (wife, born Lu(9), who married him at age 18 and died in 1148 at age 48). According to Wang Ying
2 CONC chen, who obviously considered this a marriage down for born Lu(9), the Qian and Lu were hereditarily intermarried (shiyin). In fact, Qian Xie [145] was L?Jujian's [1300] son-in-law and Lu(9) Xiji [1305] was Qian Xuan's [7142] son
2 CONC -in-law. Xiji was the elder brother of Xichun, Shouzhi's grandfather-in-law! There are no other indications that Shouzhi was related to any of the many branches of the Wuxing Qian. I am, however, assigning him as the only member o
2 CONC f a jia 'p' and as a lineal descendant of Feng [16171]. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
