1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=7055 '''Lü Zuqian''' 呂祖謙] [7055] Haowen's [8099] great grandson, Bengzhong's [1320] grandson, Han Yuanji's [669] son-in-law. Zeng Ji [1692] was the father-in-law 
2 CONC of his father, Daqi [3652]. His maternal great grandfather was Fang Meng [7220], who was also his uncle Datong's [3653] grandfather-in-law. Zuqian was a friend of Wu Fei's [1970] son, Hong [4015]. His younger brother and Zeng Ji's
2 CONC  [1692] grandson-in-law, Zujian [3655], was appointed Taifu sicheng in 1194 but was cashiered from the service and exiled to Yunzhou, a remote area of Kiangsi, in 1195 when he opposed the replacement of Chief minister of state, Zh
2 CONC ao Ruyu [3200], with Han Tuozhou [3326], Han Qi's [630] great grandson. Zujian's younger brother, Zutai [3656], who had moved from Jinhua xian to Changzhou, Yixing xian, went to the Petitioners Drum Bureau in 1196 when Zujian died
2 CONC  and petitioned that Han Tuozhou was disloyal and should be put to death in order to prevent disorder. He also asked that Su(1) Shidan [3768] be executed, Chen Ziqiang [3092] dismissed and Zhou Bida [7197] appointed Chief minister
2 CONC  of state. He was exiled to Qinzhou(b) on the coast of the South China sea, but recalled when Han Tuochou was executed. Chen Fuliang, WJ, 18.11b-12a; Lu Zuqian, WJ, 7.155-7 (jishi (wife #2 ?), born Han, who died in 1171 at age 27)
2 CONC , 8.193 (jishi (wife #3), born Rui, who died in 1179 at age 18); SHY:ZG, 73.19b-20a; Jingding Yanzhou xuzhi, 3.5a. CBD, 2, 1212-5.From Hartwell's ACTIVITY table:1169:  Arrived at post as superintendant of the Yanzhou prefectural s
2 CONC chool1170:  Replacement arrived as superintendant of Yanzhou prefectural school. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
