1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=150 '''Qian Duanli''' 錢端禮] [150] One daughter was a concubine of the heir apparent and the family regularly intermarried with the imperial clan from the early Nor
2 CONC thern Song. Duanli used his grandfather Jingchen's [7141] yin to enter the civil service. Weiyan's [8006] great great grandson, Xuan's [7142] great grandson, Chen's [7140] son, Li(2) Zhuang's [1010] son-in-law. Probably the brothe
2 CONC r or cousin of Han(1) Qiu's [632] father-in-law. His grandson, Xiangzu [3033], was in State council between 1204 and 1208 when he was despatched as prefect of Fuzhou(c). Xiangzu used Duanli's yin to enter the civil service. Duanli
2 CONC 's grandson-in-law, Wang(2) Duo [3984], was a Taizhou, Linhai resident, who earned his jinshi in 1172 and served as Tiju Guangdong shibo in 1244 and in the same year was appointed Guangdong tiju. Chicheng zhi, 33.13a, 34.21a; XNYL
2 CONC , 153.13b, 155.8a, 156.7a, 8b, 157.11a, 181.5a, 183.3a, 8b, 184.7b, 12a, 185.15b, 17b, 22a, 186.1b, 187.9b, 16a, 188.1a, 189.13a, 191.7a, 192.11b; Xianchun Linan zhi, 50.5b, 6b; XZZTJ, 138.17b, 139.3b; Guangdong TZ, 16.13a, 14a; L
