1 NAME Zi Rong /Zeng/
2 GIVN Zi Rong
2 _MARNM Zeng
1 NAME Zēng Zi Róng 曾子榮, 123, 111, 58, 54, 1世
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Zeng Zi Rong was a member of the 54th generation of the Zeng family descended from Zeng Shen.  He was the eldest son of Zeng Xing Rong.  Zi Rong moved to Sunning (Toisan), Guang Hai, Shang Ge (Sheung Gok), and was 
2 CONC the founding member of the Zeng Village.  From this was the beginning of a new branch of the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT [五十四世子榮生四子觀成、。。。徒新寧《台山》上閣居住。為新派一世開始計數。  一(五十四)世子榮公為新派一世居住曾邊。由此開族]
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the 50th generation of the Zeng Zi's family moved from Shandong to Guangdong.
2 CONT
2 CONT The founding member of the Zeng (曾) family was Zeng Shen (曾參) who was one of the most filial and devote disciples of Confucius.  Zeng Shen was born during the winter of the year of the fire monkey during the reign of King Zhou Jin
2 CONC g, on the 10th month, 12th day in current day Shandong Province in China.  He lived from 505–436 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zeng Shen (曾參) later became know as Zengzi (Tsang) (Chinese: 曾子; pinyin: Zēngzǐ; Wade-Giles: Tsengtzu), courtesy name Ziyu (子輿), was a Chinese philosopher and student of Confucius.  Zengzi is credited with authorship of a large po
2 CONC rtion of the Great Learning, including its foreword. Zengzi's disciples are believed to have been among the most important compilers of the Analects of Confucius and other Confucian classics. Zengzi was also an early Chinese propo
2 CONC nent of a round earth theory, as opposed to a flat earth model.
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zengzi
2 CONT
2 CONT Other Notes:  
2 CONT
2 CONT King Zhou Jing (aka. Ji Gai) was the twenty-sixth sovereign of the Chinese Zhou Dynasty and the fourteenth of Eastern Zhou Dynasty, and reigned from 520-476 BC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Confucius lived from 551-479 BC.
