1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=3260 '''Zhu Baoguang''' 朱葆光] [3260] Baoguang and Bi [16456] probably both moved from Changan to Nanyang and then Baoguang moved to Hengshan immediately after Five
2 CONC  Dynasty Liang Taizu changed the mandate with, according to inscription of son Ang [512] (q.v.), Tang ministers Li(2) Tao(4) [13065] and Yan Chong (not in dataset). Li Tao subsequently returned North, but Baoguang remained in Heng
2 CONC shan. The genealogical material in the inscriptions for Ang and Shu(2) [3264], along with the detailed tables in XTS (w/ only one zaixiang), suggest that kept a very detailed jiapu (Zhushi pu according to Liu Zhi). — [https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
