2 CONC milarities between the two Feng(4) suggest that they may be kin, probably Jing's father Shi and Liang are the same people since Shi is identified as Ang's son-in-law in Shi's wife's funerary inscription and only Liang is listed in
2 CONC  Ang's funerary inscription. There seems to ge a general confusion in the sources between Ma(2) Liang [1349] and Feng(4) Liang, both holding similar posts in chronological sequence. Since Shi held no office, I am going to treat al
2 CONC l references to Feng Liang as meaning Ma(2) Liang. Wife's funerary inscription identifies him as a Shiping Feng. Jiangxi TZ, 9.12a, 13b; Fujian TZ, 4.7b; XCB, 47.6a, 60.4a, 61.21a, 62.5b, 67.1a, 5b; SHY:ZG, 42.15a. Wang Gui, WJ, 5
2 CONC 5.5a-8a (wife, born Zhu, who married him at age 14 and died in 1066 at age 72). CBD, 4, 2741-2. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
