1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=7231 '''Han Yingzhou''' 韓膺冑] [7231] Zhongyan's [644] grandson, Xiaozhou's [646] brother, Xie's [647] uncle. After the fall of the Northern Song, Han(1) Qi's [630]
2 CONC  descendants scattered throughout the empire. Zhongyan died in Shaoxing and his son Zhi's [3320] two sons settled in Shaoxing. Zhi was Zhongyan's only surviving son from the first of the two daughters of Lu(9) Gongbi [1316] that h
2 CONC e married. Her first two sons died in childhood. She died at the age of 27. Yingzhou's grandson, Jing [3322], was a Suzhou jinshi in 1238, but also listed as a Shaoxing jinshi in the same year. Yingzhou was Chen(1) Anjie's [7123] 
2 CONC father-in-law. Han Qi, WJ, 48.7b; SYXA, 59.5b; YLDD, 2368.9b. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
