1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=1541 '''Sun Bian''' 孫抃] [1541] His 7th generation ancestor, by my count, Pu(2) [21386] , earned the jinshi in 845 and was an official during the reigns of Wuzong 
2 CONC and Xuanzong of Tang and was the first descendant of the Fuchun Sun to move from Fuyang-- to Changan--Su(1) Song [8116] explicitly refers to ancestry to Sun(1) Wu [20607] and then to Sun(1) Quan [20609]. See documentation for Sun(
2 CONC 1) Jian(4) [20606]. Pu held office once in Sichuan as did his son, Changru [21327], Bian's sixth generation ancestor, who also held office in Sichuan and settled in Meishan where he accumulated a large library and was known as Shu
2 CONC lou Sun shi (Book tower Mr. Sun). Changru's descendants cultivated the land and educated their sons, but did not take public office (a characteristic of the Meishan elite according to the Meishan Su). But, after a Sun(1) Kan(2) [2
2 CONC 1393], jinshi in 1019 (Sichuan TZ, 122.10a) and Bian, there were an extraordinary large number of Meishan Sun jinshi (30 before the end of the Northern Song, who must all be descendants of Changru. I have not included all of those
2 CONC  whose jinshi is only dated by multi-sitting nianhao during the Southern Song, only Shaoxing jinshi with two or more men sharing generational names. After Shaoxing, there is a long period with few Meishan jinshi until 1226 when se
2 CONC ven appear in the Sichuan TZ list, and in subsequent periods. These are not included since they may reflect the influx of unrelated Sun after the fall of the Nothern Song. Therefore the jinshi presence of this lineage is underesti
2 CONC mated for the Southern Song. Bian's wife, Wang(2) Shi, was from a great lineage (daxing) of the same address. His three sisters also married into powerful lineages of the same place (lihao) and the offspring of these unions contin
2 CONC ued to intermarry during successive generations (i.e. as members of a kindred group [yinjia]). Song(2) Fengguo's [7344] father-in-law. Sichuan TZ, 122.11a; SHY:ZG, 23.7b; SS, 292.23b-25a; Su Song, WJ, 55.10a-17a, 63.1a-18b. CBD, 3
2 CONC , 1885-6. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
